                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "pneumatic-shockmount":</h3><p>The <b>pneumatic shockmount</b> tag is reserved for Shure products that use the company&#8217;s proprietary internal &#8220;pumping&#8221; shockmount. This is a technology developed by Shure in the 1960s to reduce handling and mechanical noise in dynamic microphones. </p><p>The moving-coil cartridge is mounted in a way that allows it to move like a piston within the microphone body. The air cavities surrounding the cartridge are vented into the cavity behind the diaphragm, such that vibrations along the mic&#8217;s axis of directivity cause equal pressures to be applied to both sides of the membrane, causing cancellation. </p><p><a href="http://recordinghacks.com/2012/11/02/shure-invisible-shockmount/">Learn more about the pneumatic shockmount in this video interview.</a></p>
